       \u003Csupport>\u003Cp>Thick plaque of white marble, intact, but damaged along the upper, left and right edges.\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Cmaterial ana=\"#material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Lunense #material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Docimian #material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Hymettan #material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Pentelic\" type=\"stone.marble\" subtype=\"Lunense|Docimian|Hymettan|Pentelic\" resp=\"#Coccato\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html\">Very fine-grained, homogeneous, white marble, likely Lunense, Docimian, Hymettan, Pentelic. Digital microscopy: homeoblastic to heteroblastic fabric (identification based on pXRF, digital microscopy)\u003Cnote> Petrographic imagery at \u003Cref target=\"https://iiif.csad.ox.ac.uk/viewer/isicily/ISic000903\">https://iiif.csad.ox.ac.uk/viewer/isicily/ISic000903\u003C/ref>\u003C/note>\u003C/material>\n                                    \u003CobjectType ana=\"#object.plaque\" ref=\"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/259.html\">plaque\u003C/objectType>\n                                    \u003Cdimensions>\u003C!--from the inventory-->\n                                        \u003Cheight unit=\"cm\">10\u003C/height>\n                                        \u003Cwidth unit=\"cm\">20\u003C/width>\n                                        \u003Cdepth unit=\"cm\"/>\n                                    \u003C/dimensions>\n                                \u003C/support>\n                                \u003Ccondition ana=\"#condition.complete\"/>\n                            \u003C/supportDesc>\n                            \u003ClayoutDesc>\n                                \u003Clayout>\u003Cp>Four lines of Greek letters essentially filling the space.\u003C/p>\n                                    \u003Crs ana=\"#execution.chiselled\" ref=\"http